Apple is currently developing four models with two different designs for the iPhone's 20th anniversary, according to the leaker known as "Ice Universe."<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-18-Pro-Black.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063530" /><br/>
In a <a href="https://weibo.com/5673255066/5366561065927278">new post on Weibo</a>, the leaker outlined the two designs. Two are said to feature flat glass covers and two have glass that curves along all four edges.<br/>
<br/>
One plausible explanation for this is that Apple is developing two sizes (Pro and Pro Max models) with alternative designs, potentially retaining the flatter versions as fallbacks for the more ambitious curved design, rather than planning to launch four models. Another explanation is that the models with flat front glass are standard "iPhone 20" models set to launch after the iPhone 20 Pro.<br/>
<br/>
The curved versions reportedly have bezels measuring around 1mm, but the shape of the surrounding glass makes them almost invisible when viewed head-on, creating an almost borderless appearance. Ice Universe suggested the effect would be particularly striking in person.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has apparently been prototyping the four-sided curved glass design for three years, making several revisions during that time. The design choice is said to remain under consideration, with the earliest versions featuring substantially more pronounced curves that were later reduced.<br/>
<br/>
The report is plausible since it echoes <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/10/glass-centric-iphone-still-planned-2027/">report from August</a>, which said that Apple had scrapped an earlier, more ambitious anniversary design that used even more glass in place of metal. Gurman said the design planned for 2027 still features curved front and rear glass separated by a thin metal band. Both reports suggest Apple has moderated elements of its original design.<br/>
<br/>
The latest claims follow a series of design details about the rumored "iPhone 20 Pro" that have emerged in recent days. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/17/iphone-20-pro-screen-protectors-rumored-design/">Screen protector samples</a> circulating online show rounded edges with curves along all four sides and very narrow display borders. According to Ice Universe, the screen protectors seen in recent days reflects an early version with greater curvature.<br/>
<br/>
Earlier this week, the leaker "Fixed Focus Digital" said the devices would use <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-20-pro-to-be-based-on-iphone-air/">the same glass material as the iPhone Air</a>, but with greater curvature along all four sides. An accompanying illustration depicted rounded front and rear glass meeting a narrow, polished metal frame.<br/>
<br/>
Ice Universe added that industry sources are enthusiastic about the curved glass design, with some expressing greater anticipation for the anniversary model than for a foldable iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's 20th-anniversary iPhone models are expected to launch in the fall of 2027. While leakers have referred to the devices as the "iPhone 20 Pro," Apple's naming plans remain unclear.<br/>
